column2:
Hero, do not on this account blame the blameless maiden;
304	for she bade me follow with her handmaids,
305	but I was unwilling, fearing and being ashamed,
306	lest in some way your heart too be angered at the sight;
307	for we, the tribes of men upon the earth, are jealous.

Father Zeus, would that Alcinous might accomplish all that he said;
332	his would be unquenchable fame over the grain-giving earth,
333	and I would reach my native land.
